OTSEC harness patch for HR-23's sanitizer fuzz run (brief P4-4-HR23-FUZZ;
docs/phase4/D4-hr23-design.md, section 4.6). It changes Zeek 9.0.1's fuzz
targets only, never the code under test, and is applied alike to both
builds, C1p and C2: it adds the `dnp3_udp` target, and links the project's
CRC fix-up mutator (hr23-crc-mutator.cc, copied into src/fuzzers/) into
`dnp3_tcp`, `dnp3_udp` and `packet`; and it gives binpac's runtime library
the sanitizer and fuzzer-coverage flags libzeek has, which changes how that
library is compiled, not its source.

Against: Zeek 9.0.1, zeek-9.0.1.tar.gz (its SHA-256 is in ../build.env).
Applied from the top of the unpacked tree with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0`.

The file changed is Zeek 9.0.1's, under the BSD-3-Clause licence in
../COPYING. The lines this patch adds are the project's own (LICENSE.md).

--- a/src/fuzzers/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/fuzzers/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -105,6 +105,8 @@
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(dce_rpc)
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(dhcp udp)
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(dnp3_tcp)
+# OTSEC, HR-23's fuzz run: DNP3 over UDP, driven by NextPacket.
+add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(dnp3_udp udp)
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(dtls udp)
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(irc)
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(ldap_udp udp)
@@ -129,6 +131,21 @@
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(ssl)
 add_generic_analyzer_fuzz_target(syslog udp)
 
+# OTSEC, HR-23's fuzz run (docs/phase4/D4-hr23-design.md, section 4.6): the
+# project's CRC fix-up mutator, the same in both builds, linked into the
+# three targets the run uses. The packet target's chunks are raw IPv4
+# packets, so its copy fixes a UDP datagram's payload.
+foreach (_hr23_target zeek-dnp3_tcp-fuzzer zeek-dnp3_udp-fuzzer zeek-packet-fuzzer)
+    target_sources(${_hr23_target} PRIVATE hr23-crc-mutator.cc)
+endforeach ()
+target_compile_definitions(zeek-packet-fuzzer PRIVATE HR23_FRAMING_IP=1)
+
+# OTSEC, HR-23's fuzz run (D3's B1 on #731): binpac's runtime library, whose
+# FlowBuffer every DNP3 flow runs through, gets libzeek's sanitizer and
+# fuzzer-coverage flags. Zeek 9.0.1 names no binpac target for them, so
+# without this line the library is not instrumented.
+zeek_target_enable_sanitizers(binpac_static)
+
